#: src/dotenv-settings.md:1
msgid "Dotenv Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:3
msgid ""
"If any of `dotenv-load`, `dotenv-filename`, `dotenv-override`, `dotenv-"
"path`, or `dotenv-required` are set, `just` will try to load environment "
"variables from a file."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:7
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-path` is set, `just` will look for a file at the given path, "
"which may be absolute, or relative to the working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:10
msgid ""
"The command-line option `--dotenv-path`, short form `-E`, can be used to set "
"or override `dotenv-path` at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:13
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-filename` is set, `just` will look for a file at the given path, "
"relative to the working directory and each of its ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:16
msgid ""
"The command-line option `--dotenv-filename`, short form `-F`, can be used to "
"set or override `dotenv-filename` at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:19
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-filename` is not set, but `dotenv-load` or `dotenv-required` are "
"set, `just` will look for a file named `.env`, relative to the working "
"directory and each of its ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:23
msgid ""
"`dotenv-filename` and `dotenv-path` are similar, but `dotenv-path` is only "
"checked relative to the working directory, whereas `dotenv-filename` is "
"checked relative to the working directory and each of its ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:27
msgid ""
"It is not an error if an environment file is not found, unless `dotenv-"
"required` is set."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:30
msgid ""
"The loaded variables are environment variables, not `just` variables, and so "
"must be accessed using `$VARIABLE_NAME` in recipes and backticks."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:33
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-override` is set, variables from the environment file will "
"override existing environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:36
msgid ""
"If `dotenv-command` is set, `just` runs it with the configured `shell` and "
"loads its standard output as an environment file."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:39
msgid "This is useful for sourcing secrets from a secret manager or vault:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:45
msgid ""
"The command-line option `--dotenv-command` can be used to set or override "
"`dotenv-command` at runtime, and may be passed multiple times. Each value is "
"run as a command, with variables from later commands taking precedence over "
"variables from earlier commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:50
msgid "For example, if your `.env` file contains:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:58
msgid "And your `justfile` contains:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:60
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set dotenv-load\n"
"\n"
"serve:\n"
"  @echo \"Starting server with database $DATABASE_ADDRESS on port "
"$SERVER_PORT…\"\n"
"  ./server --database $DATABASE_ADDRESS --port $SERVER_PORT\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:68
msgid "`just serve` will output:"
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:76
msgid ""
"Variables in environment files loaded in parent modules are inherited by "
"submodules."
msgstr ""

#: src/dotenv-settings.md:79
msgid ""
"Environment files are loaded in submodules<sup>1.49.0</sup> and may override "
"variables defined in parent module environment files."
msgstr ""
